<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MasterClock core — uk (Ukrainian)

  The voice strings are spoken aloud by the phone's text-to-speech, so they are written to be heard:
  "Залишилося періодів: 3" rather than a counted noun the number would have to agree with. The
  byoyomi seconds are only ever called on a multiple of ten, which always takes "секунд".

  "Byoyomi" is spoken as "бйойомі": a mode name stays English on the screen, but a Ukrainian
  voice reads the Latin word by guesswork. TalkBack's line too.

  Written from the English, not from the Russian.

  Translated without a native reviewer, like every language here except the French.
-->
